PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
PUBLIC_MAPTILER_KEY=
# Dev override that points the map renderer at a different MapLibre
# style URL (typically a local Protomaps tileserver-gl). When set, it
# wins outright — MapTiler is bypassed and the user's style preference
# is ignored. Empty → falls back to MapTiler. For local dev this is
# already populated in the committed `.env.development` (which outranks
# `.env.local` on Vite — see decisions.md § 137); this template line is
# documentation only. Boot the server with `bin/protomaps-dev.sh start`.
# See docs/ops/protomaps_local_setup.md + decisions.md § 68 + § 137.
PUBLIC_TILE_STYLE_URL=
# OSRM routing-service base URL. Empty → falls back to the public
# https://router.project-osrm.org demo server (rate-limited, sometimes
# overloaded). Set to a self-hosted instance for production-quality
# turn-by-turn snapping; the apps/job_worker/osrm/ recipe and the
# `npm run dev:run:osrm` helper script provision one locally.
PUBLIC_OSRM_URL=
# Self-hosted GraphHopper base URL for SERVER-SIDE distance-targeted
# route-loop generation (`/api/routes/generate`, decisions §137). Note
# the absence of the PUBLIC_ prefix — this is SERVER-ONLY so the browser
# never reaches the engine and the user's start coordinates never leave
# our infra (privacy parity with the self-hosted OSRM map-matcher).
# Unset → the endpoint returns 501 and the route builder falls back to
# the in-browser OSRM radial heuristic. GraphHopper is loop-generation
# only; OSRM (above) still owns snapping + map-matching.
GRAPHHOPPER_URL=
# Shared secret sent to GraphHopper as the X-Engine-Key header. The engine sits
# behind a public Fly endpoint with a Caddy guard that rejects requests without
# the matching key (the AWS Lambda can't reach it over Fly's private network).
# SERVER-ONLY. Prod: a real secret via sops → the Lambda env, set as a Fly app
# secret on the GraphHopper side. Local dev uses a committed value (see
# .env.development). Unset → no header sent (guard must be permissive).
GRAPHHOPPER_API_KEY=
# graph_cycle sidecar (apps/graph_cycle) — the v3 graph-cycle loop generator,
# tried FIRST by /api/routes/generate ahead of GraphHopper. SERVER-ONLY (no
# PUBLIC_), same privacy posture as GRAPHHOPPER_URL. Unset → the handler skips
# graph-cycle and uses GraphHopper round_trip / the in-browser OSRM heuristic.
GRAPH_CYCLE_URL=
# Shared secret sent to the sidecar as X-Engine-Key (its in-process guard checks
# it, fail-closed). SERVER-ONLY. Prod: a real secret via sops → the Lambda env,
# set as a Fly app secret on the sidecar. Unset → no header sent (dev only).
GRAPH_CYCLE_API_KEY=
# Strava OAuth — public client ID is embedded in the redirect URL; the
# non-PUBLIC client id + secret live ONLY in apps/backend/.env.example
# (the Edge Function reads them at runtime). They were here once and
# the audit-secrets pass flagged them as misleading — the web bundle
# doesn't read either, so setting them in apps/web/.env.local is a
# no-op that creates false confidence.
PUBLIC_STRAVA_CLIENT_ID=
# USDA FoodData Central — second nutrition food-search source, queried
# CLIENT-SIDE from the browser (api.nal.usda.gov), alongside the keyless
# Open Food Facts source. The key is low-sensitivity (a free FDC sign-up,
# rate-limited per key) so it ships PUBLIC_; even so it's gated FAIL-CLOSED:
# unset → the USDA source is simply not queried and Open Food Facts still
# works, no error, no broken composer. USDA = a new outbound personal-data
# flow (the search term leaves the browser) — see the nutrition
# pre-real-user-launch privacy checklist + decisions §188 before going live.
PUBLIC_USDA_FDC_API_KEY=
# RevenueCat hosted Pro checkout (optional). The web Pro flow redirects
# to RevenueCat's hosted surfaces instead of embedding the JS SDK, so no
# secret/API key lives in the browser — just the two public redirect URLs
# below. When the CHECKOUT URL is unset, the "Get Pro" CTA on
# /settings/upgrade falls back to a "coming soon" toast instead of opening
# a real checkout (the `configured = false` fail-closed path).
#
# Web Paywall Link base of the form https://pay.rev.cat/<token>. The app
# appends the URL-encoded Supabase user id as the App User ID path segment
# and a redirect_url back to /settings/upgrade.
PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_WEB_CHECKOUT_URL=
# No-code customer-portal link for managing/cancelling a web subscription
# (RevenueCat authenticates the user by email at the portal). Backs the
# "Manage subscription" button. Unset → that button shows a "manage where
# you started it" hint.
PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_WEB_PORTAL_URL=
# Go live-hub base URL — e.g. https://live.threkir.com. When set,
# `/live/[id]` opens a WebSocket to
# `${PUBLIC_LIVE_HUB_URL}/v1/live/{run_id}/subscribe` for real-time
# spectator pings instead of the Supabase Realtime channel on
# `live_run_pings`. Empty → falls back to the legacy Realtime path.
# See `apps/web/src/lib/live_hub.ts` + `apps/job_worker/internal/livehub/`.
PUBLIC_LIVE_HUB_URL=
# Go service base URL for the cloud-export endpoint. Same host as
# PUBLIC_LIVE_HUB_URL in production (the Go service hosts both
# /v1/live and /v1/export). When set, the Settings → Data Export
# "Cloud export (GPX zip)" button POSTs to `${PUBLIC_EXPORT_HUB_URL}/v1/export`
# instead of the legacy `export-data` Edge Function. Empty → falls
# back to the EF. See `apps/web/src/lib/cloud_export.ts`.
PUBLIC_EXPORT_HUB_URL=
# Canonical site URL used by the prerendered /sitemap.xml. The build
# bakes this into every <loc>, so preview and prod each emit their
# own host. Unset → defaults to https://threkir.com (matches prod).
PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
# Supabase service-role key (SERVER-ONLY — never PUBLIC_, never in the
# client bundle). The coach handler uses it to persist the assistant
# message: since migration 20261122_001 the coach_messages INSERT policy
# only allows clients to write role='user' rows (XSS audit H1), so the
# assistant turn is written by this RLS-bypassing role. Unset → assistant
# messages aren't persisted (the reply still streams). In production it is
# provisioned via the env's sops secrets file (infra/modules/web-stack).
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Coach provider switch. `anthropic` (default, prod) or `openai` for any
# OpenAI-compatible /v1 endpoint (Ollama, llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio).
# When set to `openai`, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is ignored.
COACH_PROVIDER=anthropic
# Only used when COACH_PROVIDER=openai. Defaults below match a local
# Ollama install (`ollama serve` on :11434, model pulled via `ollama pull`).
OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
OPENAI_API_KEY=ollama
OPENAI_MODEL=llama3.2
# Web push (optional). Generate a VAPID keypair (e.g. `npx web-push
# generate-vapid-keys`); the PUBLIC half lives in the browser bundle to
# subscribe with, the PRIVATE half lives in the Edge Function env to
# sign push payloads. Without these the "Notifications" card on
# /settings/account renders a "not configured" hint instead of the
# Enable button.
PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# Sentry (optional). The PUBLIC_ DSN is the browser SDK's; the
# server-side SENTRY_DSN is injected at runtime by the Lambda env
# (sops-encrypted) — not needed in apps/web/.env.local for local dev.
# PUBLIC_APP_RELEASE is set by the release-web.yml CI step to the
# git tag (`web@1.2.3`) so Sentry can correlate errors to a specific
# build; leave blank locally.
PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
PUBLIC_APP_RELEASE=
# BYPASS_PAYWALL is kept out of THIS template (.env.example is a copy-me
# starting point that could be mistaken for a prod config). It IS set in the
# committed `.env.development`, which Vite loads only for `vite dev` — never
# for the prod `vite build` — so the free seed user can exercise Pro features
# locally. The `/api/coach` dev wrapper accepts it only when all are true:
#   - NODE_ENV is not 'production'
#   - PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL points at the local stack (127.0.0.1 / localhost)
#   - the literal string 'true'
# Production is the AWS Lambda, which hardcodes the bypass off.
#
# Client-side companion `PUBLIC_BYPASS_PAYWALL` opens the UI-gate
# (`isLocked()` in `$lib/features.ts`) for free users on a dev machine
# so the `<ProGate>` lock-card doesn't block local iteration on /coach.
# Same three-condition AND on the client (`import.meta.env.DEV` +
# local Supabase URL + literal 'true').
#
# Race-director weigh-in / medical UI gate (Art 9 health data, fail-closed —
# race_director_ops.md P3, decisions §150). The body-weight + medical-hold +
# consent surface on the checkpoint board is HIDDEN unless this is explicitly
# truthy (1 / true / yes / on). Unset / empty / anything else → off, so health
# data can't be collected on the web until owner + CISO + counsel sign-off
# flips it at deploy time. The DB also gates persistence (requires_weigh_in +
# p_health_consent), so this is the client half of a defence-in-depth pair.
PUBLIC_WEIGH_IN_ENABLED=

# AI Coach gate — one of the two Pro storefront gates (the other is
# PUBLIC_ROUTE_GEN_ENABLED below; Pro is sellable when either perk is live).
# When the Coach is off (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY unset → /api/coach 503s, the
# rock-bottom deploy) every Coach entry point hides and the Pro card drops its
# Coach bullets. Set truthy (1 / true / yes / on) only when the Coach is live;
# unset / empty / anything else → off. With BOTH gates off /settings/upgrade
# shows a "Pro — coming soon" teaser and leads with donations instead of
# selling a hollow subscription. paywall.md.
PUBLIC_COACH_ENABLED=

# Server route generation gate — the second Pro storefront gate (decisions
# §204). Server-side loop generation (graph_cycle + GraphHopper) is a Pro perk;
# the free tier keeps the in-browser heuristic. The real gate is server-side
# (engine URLs unset → 501; free caller → 403); this flag is the client half —
# it shows the /routes/new upsell and the Pro-card bullet. Set truthy only once
# the Fly engines are actually standing (deferred on rock-bottom AND Lean,
# deployment_lean.md); unset / empty / anything else → off.
PUBLIC_ROUTE_GEN_ENABLED=
